        "calls": 2,
        "title": "Add CLI flow attribution to Freebuff login and define auth step",
        "summary": "The CLI now appends a `cli_flow` query parameter to the Freebuff sign-in URL to attribute sessions back to the command line interface. This mechanism is gated behind the `IS_FREEBUFF` constant so that the paid Codebuff product remains unchanged. In the shared package, a new `freebuff-auth-funnel.ts` module introduces Zod schemas and helpers for a low-volume `freebuff.auth_step` recovery funnel, which is added to the `ALWAYS_TRACK_EVENTS` set in `analytics-sampling.ts` to ensure these events are never randomly dropped. The change also includes a few minor formatting adjustments in the plain-text login flow.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "maintainers",
        "evidence": "In `cli/src/login/login-flow.ts`, the new `withCliLoginFlow` function and `cliFlowId` option allow appending a `cli_flow` query parameter to the login URL. Additionally, `common/src/constants/freebuff-auth-funnel.ts` is a new file defining schemas for `freebuff.auth_step`, and `common/src/util/analytics-sampling.ts` adds `FREEBUFF_AUTH_STEP` to `ALWAYS_TRACK_EVENTS`.",
        "userVisible": false,
        "confidence": "medium",
        "unknowns": "The diff shows the CLI-side implementation and schema but not the web or desktop surface that will consume the `auth_step` events or the new correlation identifiers.",
