        "calls": 1,
        "title": "Add new-user ad ramp fields to Axiom fetch log",
        "summary": "The shared Axiom log allowlist in `common` extends the `ads.fetch_completed` event schema with six new fields tracking the new-user ad ramp experiment (COD-904). These fields capture the ramp outcome, arm assignment, session index, suppression flag, keep probability in basis points, and signup day, while `no_fill_reason` gains a `new_user_ramp` code to record when the ramp withholds an ad request. The mechanism ensures these operational signals are preserved in Axiom for dashboards without entering product analytics, as defined by the allowlist in `axiom-only-log.ts`.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "audience": "operators",
        "evidence": "The diff in `common/src/util/axiom-only-log.ts` adds six new fields (`new_user_ramp_outcome`, `new_user_ramp_arm`, `session_index`, `new_user_ramp_suppressed`, `new_user_ramp_keep_bps`, `new_user_signup_day`) to `ADS_FETCH_COMPLETED_FIELDS` and adds `new_user_ramp` to the documented `no_fill_reason` codes, supporting the new-user ad ramp experiment (COD-904).",
